# Cursor Rules for AMS Client (Academy Management System)

You are an expert Next.js, React 19, and TypeScript engineer working on `ams-client`.

## Tech Stack
- Next.js 16 (App Router with Server Components)
- React 19 & React DOM 19
- TypeScript 5 (Strict Mode, path alias `@/*` -> `./src/*`)
- CSS Modules + Base UI (`@base-ui/react`) + Lucide Icons (`lucide-react`)
- Tokens from `src/styles/tokens.css` (Style Dictionary)

## Golden Rules
1. **Never alter UI or visual styles without explicit user instruction.**
2. **Never place `.module.css` files directly in `src/app/`.** Keep `src/app/` minimal and clean.
3. Feature code belongs in `src/features/<feature>/` (`components/`, `services/`, `types/`).
4. Shared UI belongs in `src/components/ui/` or `src/components/layout/`.
5. Run `pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm lint` after making changes to verify 0 errors.

## Palette & Tokens
- DSCA Brand: `#028c4a`
- GBTA Brand: `#ff7724`
- Action Primary: `#1b84ff` / `--ams-color-primary-300`
- Text Primary: `#071437` / `--ams-color-grayscale-400`
- Text Muted: `#99a1b7` / `--ams-color-grayscale-300`
- Touch Ripple: `@/lib/touch-ripple`
